WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.400
Most pathways you have met work by adding something, such as a phosphate or a second

2
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.000
messenger. Hedgehog works the other way.

3
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:15.020
It tells the cells of an embryo where they are by switching off an off-switch.

4
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.740
To follow it, you need one piece of logic.

5
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:19.980
That logic is called a double negative.

6
00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:24.873
Two proteins in the membrane of the receiving cell receive the signal.

7
00:00:25.593 --> 00:00:28.653
Patched is a brake, and Smoothened is the protein that it keeps off.

8
00:00:29.313 --> 00:00:32.813
With no Hedgehog, Patched is active, so Smoothened is off.

9
00:00:33.553 --> 00:00:35.193
Patched does not hold Smoothened.

10
00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:38.193
One Patched can keep many Smoothened molecules quiet.

11
00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:42.247
Now Hedgehog arrives and binds Patched, to the brake.

12
00:00:42.987 --> 00:00:44.647
Hedgehog does not press the accelerator.

13
00:00:45.247 --> 00:00:46.607
It releases the handbrake.

14
00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:49.567
Patched is switched off, so Smoothened is on.

15
00:00:50.207 --> 00:00:54.087
Hedgehog switches off the protein that keeps Smoothened off, and that is the double

16
00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:55.087
negative.

17
00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.580
The pathway ends at a transcription factor called Gli.

18
00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.940
With Smoothened off, kinases add phosphates to Gli, and ubiquitin tags it for the

19
00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:08.800
proteasome. The proteasome destroys only its back part, which holds the activating

20
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:14.020
region. The front part still binds DNA, and as a repressor it keeps the Hedgehog

21
00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:19.120
target genes off. With Smoothened on, the marking stops, and Gli stays whole and

22
00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:20.120
becomes an activator.

23
00:01:21.083 --> 00:01:24.363
In vertebrates, this pathway runs at the primary cilium.

24
00:01:25.003 --> 00:01:29.183
Many kinds of cell carry one, a single hair-like projection that does not beat.

25
00:01:29.743 --> 00:01:33.383
Without Hedgehog, Patched sits at the cilium and Smoothened stays out.

26
00:01:33.943 --> 00:01:37.203
When Hedgehog binds, Patched leaves and Smoothened moves in.

27
00:01:37.923 --> 00:01:41.463
Gli proteins gathered at the tip of the cilium are sent to the nucleus as

28
00:01:41.463 --> 00:01:42.463
activators.

29
00:01:43.117 --> 00:01:46.937
Now use that logic to predict what happens when a part of the pathway is lost.

30
00:01:47.677 --> 00:01:52.177
With no Patched, nothing restrains Smoothened, so the pathway is on, with or without

31
00:01:52.177 --> 00:01:57.257
Hedgehog. With no Smoothened, nothing passes the signal on, so the pathway is off

32
00:01:57.257 --> 00:02:02.137
both ways. With neither protein the pathway is off as well, because the later step

33
00:02:02.137 --> 00:02:06.817
decides. So ask what state Smoothened is in, and everything after it follows.
